TASK: Expand the Medical Knowledge RAG using the official MedlinePlus XML topic dataset

PROJECT:
healthcare-agentic-ai

OBJECTIVE:
Replace the current tiny MedlinePlus medical corpus (currently 3 MedlinePlus documents / 17 chunks, 5 total medical documents / 87 chunks including PMC) with the full official MedlinePlus English health-topic XML dataset.

OFFICIAL SOURCE:
https://medlineplus.gov/xml/mplus_topics_2026-09-22.xml

IMPORTANT:
This is a corpus-ingestion expansion task.

Do NOT change:
- Phase 4 architecture
- Phase 5 architecture
- Phase 6 safety policy
- Diagnostic Agent safety behavior
- Clinical Critic behavior
- Safety Validator rules
- DDXPlus parser
- Patient Case RAG
- BGE model
- existing provider configuration
- GPT-5.6-Sol configuration
- patient-case labels/provenance protections

The purpose is ONLY to expand and improve the Medical Knowledge RAG corpus.

============================================================
1. INSPECT THE EXISTING MEDICAL RAG
============================================================

Before modifying anything:

Inspect the existing implementation and determine:

- current medical ingestion scripts
- XML/API parsers
- document model
- chunking implementation
- embedding implementation
- Qdrant collection configuration
- metadata schema
- existing MedlinePlus ingestion
- existing PMC ingestion
- medical retriever
- focused_medical.py
- medical RAG tests
- current Qdrant collection name/path
- current index fingerprint mechanism

Do not duplicate existing functionality unnecessarily.

Reuse existing embedding/chunking/Qdrant infrastructure wherever possible.

============================================================
2. DOWNLOAD THE OFFICIAL XML PROGRAMMATICALLY
============================================================

Add a reproducible ingestion script, for example:

scripts/ingest_medlineplus.py

It must download:

https://medlineplus.gov/xml/mplus_topics_2026-09-22.xml

Do NOT require the user to manually download the XML.

Use a normal HTTP client already compatible with the project.

Requirements:

- reasonable timeout
- clear error message on HTTP/download failure
- verify successful HTTP response
- write the downloaded XML to a deterministic local raw-data location such as:

data/medical/raw/medlineplus/mplus_topics_2026-09-22.xml

Do not commit the raw XML to source control.

If the file already exists and its checksum matches the downloaded file, support reuse without downloading unnecessarily.

Record:
- source URL
- retrieval date/time
- file size
- SHA-256
- dataset filename/version

Do not silently use a different MedlinePlus source.

============================================================
3. PARSE THE XML
============================================================

Inspect the actual XML schema before implementing the parser.

Parse ALL valid English health-topic records available in this file.

Do not hard-code a small list of topics.

For each topic, preserve useful source metadata such as:

- topic identifier
- title
- URL
- language if available
- source/update metadata if available
- associated health information
- other useful structured fields present in the XML

Extract actual medical content rather than indexing XML markup.

Do not embed:
- XML tags
- navigation markup
- irrelevant formatting
- duplicate boilerplate
- empty fields

Preserve meaningful section boundaries where the XML provides them.

Do not invent missing medical information.

============================================================
4. DOCUMENT NORMALIZATION
============================================================

Create normalized medical documents with a schema similar to:

{
    "source": "medlineplus",
    "document_id": "...",
    "title": "...",
    "url": "...",
    "language": "en",
    "source_version": "2026-09-22",
    "text": "...",
    "metadata": {...}
}

Use deterministic document IDs.

The same XML input must produce the same document IDs.

Do not include patient diagnosis labels or DDXPlus labels.

============================================================
5. CHUNKING
============================================================

Use the project's existing chunking strategy if appropriate.

Do NOT merely split every existing document into extremely tiny pieces just to inflate the chunk count.

Chunks must represent meaningful medical passages.

Prefer section-aware chunking where possible.

Each chunk must preserve:

- deterministic chunk ID
- parent document ID
- source
- title
- URL
- section if available
- source version
- chunk text

Avoid duplicate or near-empty chunks.

Make chunking deterministic.

Document the chunking parameters.

============================================================
6. EMBEDDINGS
============================================================

Reuse the existing:

BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5

Do NOT introduce another embedding model.

Maintain the existing embedding dimensionality and distance metric.

Do not download a new model if the existing cached model is available.

Track:

- embedding model
- embedding dimension
- chunk count
- embedding failures
- truncation count

Fail closed if embedding generation silently loses documents.

============================================================
7. QDRANT INDEX
============================================================

Do NOT blindly append the new MedlinePlus corpus to the existing collection.

Build a reproducible medical index.

Preferred behavior:

1. Preserve the existing PMC source ingestion capability.
2. Rebuild the medical collection from:
   - full MedlinePlus XML corpus
   - existing authorized PMC corpus
3. Replace the previous 87-chunk index with the expanded index.

Ensure that deterministic IDs prevent duplicates.

Keep patient-case Qdrant collection completely separate.

DO NOT modify the patient-case collection.

============================================================
8. PROVENANCE AND LICENSING
============================================================

Every MedlinePlus chunk must retain enough metadata to reconstruct its origin.

At minimum:

source = "medlineplus"
document_id
chunk_id
title
url
source_version
language

If the existing schema supports license/provenance metadata, preserve it.

Do not claim licensing information that is not explicitly supported by the source.

============================================================
9. RETRIEVAL COMPATIBILITY
============================================================

The existing medical retriever must continue working.

The current Phase 6 focused retrieval behavior must remain compatible.

For example, the current query:

pediatric female detachment; sweating; cramp; chest pain; flank; hypochondrium; breast; shortness of breath; choking; fear of dying; palpitations; numbness tingling history: anxiety; family psychiatric illness; depression; asthma clinical information red flags

should be able to retrieve relevant medical topics from the expanded corpus.

Do not weaken the existing concept-overlap filtering merely to increase recall.

Do not remove safety filtering.

